avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-12T14:37:04Z","updated_at":"2024-12-12T14:37:04Z","body":"> IMO this should be considered a codestyle improvement before being regarded as a performance optimization. \r\n\r\nIf this was a codestyle change instead of an optimization, it would be a bad one because it increases the complexity of the code :)\r\n\r\n> It's a best practice stuff. Not every `reserve` result in considerable performance gain, but by enforcing this style, we can avoid accidentally writing poorly performing code.\r\n\r\nI agree it's good practice to call `reserve` when the expected size is known.\r\nAnd it's good practice _because_ of performance considerations. If it was _always_ of negligible benefit to call `reserve`, we wouldn't do it.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2539132801/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]